WEBVTT

00:41.291 --> 00:43.961
NO TAIL TO TELL

00:48.882 --> 00:50.259
And as for you.

00:50.801 --> 00:52.386
I'll be coming for you soon.

00:54.471 --> 00:55.806
No!

01:04.648 --> 01:05.816
Mr. Lee.

01:07.067 --> 01:08.860
Hey. Did you get it?

01:09.611 --> 01:10.696
Yes, sir.

01:11.989 --> 01:13.865
But what do you need this for?

01:13.949 --> 01:14.992
Move, damn it.

01:28.422 --> 01:32.301
I was… thinking about this all wrong.

01:33.385 --> 01:34.553
Pardon?

01:34.636 --> 01:37.347
I'm done shaking like an idiot

01:38.181 --> 01:40.142
over those wretched things.

01:41.393 --> 01:44.730
Sorcery, spirits, whatever.
I'll just shoot them all dead.

01:50.152 --> 01:51.361
We humans

01:53.030 --> 01:54.948
have our own ways.

02:07.127 --> 02:11.214
EPISODE 11
THE WAY OF HUMANS

02:12.424 --> 02:15.302
THIRTY HOURS AGO

02:17.095 --> 02:18.180
SUNCHEON STADIUM

02:26.438 --> 02:27.314
Eun-ho.

02:31.026 --> 02:32.361
Are you okay?

02:44.456 --> 02:45.457
What's wrong?

02:50.087 --> 02:51.463
I don't know.

02:52.089 --> 02:53.924
I think it was just a dream.

02:54.716 --> 02:56.218
It has to be.

02:58.720 --> 03:01.098
I guess I'm just anxious.

03:03.183 --> 03:04.434
Anxious about what?

03:06.061 --> 03:07.104
It's just…

03:09.022 --> 03:10.816
This isn't just a breeze.

03:11.650 --> 03:13.735
A storm is about to hit.

03:16.697 --> 03:18.281
What are you thinking about?

03:19.324 --> 03:20.784
- What?
- Man…

03:20.867 --> 03:23.120
Anyway, what happened to the coach?

03:24.788 --> 03:27.499
The game's about to start.
Why isn't he here yet?

03:27.582 --> 03:29.876
We don't even have a starting lineup.

03:32.254 --> 03:34.840
Don't you think
Coach has been acting weird lately?

03:35.632 --> 03:37.509
Do you think he got a scouting offer?

03:38.260 --> 03:41.096
Is he dumping us mid-season
for another team?

03:41.179 --> 03:43.473
Don't talk nonsense.

03:44.141 --> 03:45.684
Guys, it's not like that.

03:45.767 --> 03:48.103
Why not? It could happen.

03:48.645 --> 03:52.232
He's right. Sure, Coach has always
ranked last in the fourth division,

03:52.315 --> 03:57.320
and his playing career wasn't remarkable.
His tactics are old-school,

03:57.946 --> 03:59.948
his training predictable,

04:00.031 --> 04:02.451
but that doesn't mean
he couldn't get an offer.

04:02.534 --> 04:04.202
You know, Si-yeol,

04:04.286 --> 04:07.706
you have a habit of looking down
on our coach way too much.

04:08.874 --> 04:10.667
Whoa! Hi, Coach.

04:10.751 --> 04:12.878
Why don't you just badmouth me,
you punk?

04:12.961 --> 04:15.547
Coach, why are you so late?

04:16.173 --> 04:17.632
What about the starting lineup?

04:17.716 --> 04:19.468
We don't even have any tactics,

04:19.551 --> 04:22.179
and we haven't analyzed
the opposing team at all.

04:22.262 --> 04:23.597
How are we supposed to play?

04:23.680 --> 04:25.098
Forget that. Don't worry too much.

04:25.182 --> 04:28.143
Anyway, that's not what matters today.

04:28.226 --> 04:30.270
I have a really important announcement.

04:31.146 --> 04:32.355
What?

04:32.898 --> 04:35.108
What are you doing out there?
Come on in.

04:40.238 --> 04:44.201
From now on, she'll be working
with our team as our new GM.

04:44.284 --> 04:45.744
This is Ms. Hong Yeon-su.

04:45.827 --> 04:47.537
Come on. Let's give her a hand.

04:51.333 --> 04:53.960
Okay… but Coach,

04:54.044 --> 04:55.378
the game's about to start,

04:55.462 --> 04:58.256
and this is supposed to be
your big announcement?

04:58.340 --> 05:02.010
Not exactly. There's something else.

05:02.093 --> 05:05.639
Well, what's your match fee these days?

05:05.722 --> 05:08.016
It's… 50,000 won.

05:08.099 --> 05:10.727
- Right. And your win bonus?
- It's 300,000 won.

05:12.270 --> 05:14.815
Starting today, our players' match fee

05:14.898 --> 05:17.901
won't be 50,000 won anymore.
It will be 200,000 won.

05:18.568 --> 05:19.611
Did she say 200,000 won?

05:19.694 --> 05:21.655
- It's 200,000 won?
- 200,000?

05:22.572 --> 05:24.616
And the win bonus went up a bit too.

05:25.742 --> 05:27.369
How much?

05:30.330 --> 05:31.456
One million won.

05:37.212 --> 05:38.463
For real?

05:38.547 --> 05:39.798
What…

05:41.299 --> 05:43.426
- Oh yeah!
- One million won!

05:49.349 --> 05:51.393
Hey, hang on. Quiet!

05:51.476 --> 05:53.603
Coach, is this for real?

05:54.688 --> 05:57.399
- Of course it is!
- Yeah!

05:58.358 --> 06:00.527
Hey! Are you guys ready
to play for real today?

06:00.610 --> 06:01.945
- Yes!
- Yes!

06:02.028 --> 06:03.905
- Do you need tactics?
- No!

06:03.989 --> 06:06.616
- Do we need to analyze the other team?
- No!

06:06.700 --> 06:08.368
All right, let's go!

06:12.330 --> 06:14.583
Hey! We're going positionless!

06:14.666 --> 06:16.877
- Let's do it!
- Show them how it's done!

06:19.504 --> 06:21.089
DAEHEUNG WINS ANYTIME, ANYWHERE

06:21.172 --> 06:23.216
Maybe it's because
I heard all that crappy nonsense.

06:23.300 --> 06:25.886
I can't believe I had
that stupid dream again.

06:25.969 --> 06:28.555
It's starting to get to me.

06:28.638 --> 06:29.556
Okay. One, two!

06:29.639 --> 06:32.392
- Daeheung, Daeheung, let's go!
- Daeheung, Daeheung, let's go!

06:32.475 --> 06:34.895
- Let's go!
- There's Si-yeol.

06:42.235 --> 06:43.904
- Suncheon!
- Suncheon!

06:45.572 --> 06:46.990
- Suncheon!
- Suncheon!

06:47.073 --> 06:50.994
What's gotten into them today?

06:51.077 --> 06:53.079
I dangled some money in front of them.

06:54.623 --> 06:58.251
Look at them. They're full of energy now.

06:58.335 --> 07:00.879
They're running around like excited mutts.

07:03.882 --> 07:05.342
- You…
- My bad.

07:06.301 --> 07:07.510
I forgot to tell you

07:08.011 --> 07:10.472
that I'm now the owner of that loser club.

07:11.681 --> 07:12.641
The owner?

07:14.809 --> 07:15.894
I did some digging,

07:15.977 --> 07:18.897
and you seem pretty tight
with Kang Si-yeol over there.

07:19.814 --> 07:23.860
Funnily enough, he and I go way back too.

07:23.944 --> 07:25.403
I'm sure

07:26.696 --> 07:28.156
you're already aware of that.

07:31.326 --> 07:33.203
You're acting pretty cocky today.

07:33.286 --> 07:37.874
Last time we met,
you couldn't even look me in the eye.

07:40.210 --> 07:42.337
Not anymore.

07:42.921 --> 07:44.130
I heard

07:44.881 --> 07:46.633
you're just an ordinary human now.

07:50.053 --> 07:54.599
You know, I've got to admit
that I was terrified of you.

07:54.683 --> 07:58.395
I never knew when you'd show up
or what you'd do,

07:58.478 --> 08:02.190
so I just hid like a scared little coward.

08:02.273 --> 08:05.276
Man, that felt…

08:07.112 --> 08:08.321
like absolute shit.

08:10.073 --> 08:11.616
What are you plotting?

08:11.700 --> 08:14.828
I'm just here to let you know
that things have changed.

08:20.417 --> 08:22.377
You must've enjoyed looking down on us,

08:22.460 --> 08:25.880
toying with people
like it was all a game to you.

08:26.548 --> 08:28.216
But now it's my turn.

08:28.758 --> 08:30.427
Here in the human world,

08:30.510 --> 08:35.056
I'll show you how hellish life can get
when you cross someone like me.

08:36.474 --> 08:39.561
Luckily, I still have that much sway.

08:45.734 --> 08:47.694
- Yeah!
- Yeah!

08:49.029 --> 08:51.614
Coach, we won a million won!

08:51.698 --> 08:54.534
A million won! I can't believe this!

08:54.617 --> 08:56.077
It's a million won!

08:56.161 --> 08:57.620
- Unbelievable!
- A million won!

08:58.496 --> 09:01.374
I'm going to start
by targeting the people around you,

09:01.458 --> 09:03.084
one by one.

09:03.918 --> 09:04.794
What?

09:04.878 --> 09:07.839
Where's the fun
in ending things so quickly?

09:09.090 --> 09:11.301
Now that the tables have turned,

09:11.926 --> 09:14.637
don't you think it's only fair
for me to toy with you?

09:17.891 --> 09:19.017
Hey, did you see that?

09:19.100 --> 09:23.146
I want you to be terrified,
never knowing when I'll strike,

09:23.646 --> 09:26.858
feeling like shit
for being such a pathetic mess.

09:42.707 --> 09:43.666
We're going to kill her.

09:45.126 --> 09:46.377
- Hey!
- What?

09:46.461 --> 09:47.921
- Hey!
- What's wrong?

09:49.464 --> 09:50.548
What are you doing, Si-yeol?

09:50.632 --> 09:51.925
Si-yeol!

09:52.008 --> 09:54.177
Man, this is fun already.

09:55.095 --> 09:56.971
- Are you okay?
- Yeah.

09:58.848 --> 10:00.767
- Oh boy.
- What do you want?

10:01.476 --> 10:03.728
Is this allowed when the game's still on?

10:03.812 --> 10:07.357
Tell me why you keep
lurking around Eun-ho!

10:07.440 --> 10:08.733
You know why.

10:08.817 --> 10:11.236
I have a score to settle with that fox.

10:11.319 --> 10:12.654
You bastard.

10:14.030 --> 10:15.281
Oh my God!

10:16.032 --> 10:18.451
Hey, what the hell
do you think you're doing?

10:18.535 --> 10:20.120
Man, that hurts.

10:20.203 --> 10:21.788
Sir, are you okay?

10:22.413 --> 10:24.999
You really need to control
your players better, Coach.

10:25.667 --> 10:28.336
He's not an athlete. He's a total thug.

10:28.419 --> 10:29.337
You little--

10:30.421 --> 10:32.632
- Hey.
- Come on.

10:32.715 --> 10:33.967
Oh my. You're bleeding.

10:35.677 --> 10:37.804
Seriously, what was that?

10:38.346 --> 10:41.558
We started off strong,
so I thought we'd win.

10:41.641 --> 10:42.559
Si-yeol!

10:42.642 --> 10:45.395
Where is he? Where is that bastard?

10:45.478 --> 10:46.688
- Coach!
- No, Coach!

10:46.771 --> 10:48.898
- Si-yeol, you…
- Whoa, calm down.

10:48.982 --> 10:50.358
Si-yeol isn't here.

10:50.441 --> 10:52.193
- He's not? Okay, fine.
- Si-yeol's gone.

10:52.277 --> 10:54.279
So where did
that bastard go then?

10:54.946 --> 10:55.905
Well,

10:56.447 --> 10:58.700
I think he left early
after getting the red card.

11:00.618 --> 11:01.953
What? He left?

11:02.704 --> 11:06.708
Wow, the least he could do is
get on his knees and beg for forgiveness,

11:06.791 --> 11:08.001
but he just left?

11:08.543 --> 11:10.378
Seriously, is he nuts?

11:10.461 --> 11:13.882
I'm sure he left because he felt
too embarrassed to face us--

11:13.965 --> 11:17.218
Sure! That jerk has it real easy, right?

11:17.302 --> 11:19.429
He has amazing team spirit.

11:19.512 --> 11:21.848
Hey, I'm tearing up.
Seriously, I'm so moved.

11:23.892 --> 11:25.643
But you know what?

11:25.727 --> 11:29.397
Thanks to Si-yeol, our team is screwed.

11:29.480 --> 11:30.773
Come on, Coach.

11:30.857 --> 11:34.027
I mean, Si-yeol did mess up,
but I'm sure it's not that bad.

11:34.110 --> 11:36.362
We'll do better in our next match.

11:36.446 --> 11:38.531
Oh, sure.
Just do better in the next match.

11:38.615 --> 11:43.453
Right. But do you know
who Si-yeol beat up today?

11:45.914 --> 11:48.082
He was none other than

11:49.000 --> 11:51.211
our new club owner.

11:53.922 --> 11:57.759
A member of the family
that owns Geumsu Group!

11:57.842 --> 12:01.304
Wait, hold on. A billionaire?

12:01.387 --> 12:05.433
Wait, does that mean our team
is owned by a huge conglomerate?

12:05.516 --> 12:06.976
Not anymore, you idiot!

12:07.060 --> 12:10.230
Because of Si-yeol, the deal is off!

12:11.564 --> 12:14.692
Your 200,000-won match fee

12:14.776 --> 12:17.403
and the million-won win bonus
are all gone.

12:17.487 --> 12:21.783
And since we have no sponsor,
our team really is shutting down for good!

12:22.367 --> 12:24.035
Si-yeol, that bastard!

12:24.118 --> 12:27.664
He punched the new club owner
right in the face!

12:27.747 --> 12:29.374
And he landed a direct hit!

12:29.457 --> 12:31.918
Guys! What am I supposed to do now?

12:32.001 --> 12:33.461
I'm going to kill…

12:33.544 --> 12:35.588
- Hey…
- Coach! Your knees!

12:35.672 --> 12:37.632
Hey! Call 911!

12:37.715 --> 12:39.759
SUNCHEON STATION

12:48.017 --> 12:50.520
- Where are we going?
- Straight back to Seoul.

12:51.604 --> 12:53.356
What's going to change if we leave?

12:54.399 --> 12:55.858
I know, but…

12:56.693 --> 12:59.112
You know what kind of guy he is.

12:59.195 --> 13:00.947
He tried to kill you back then.

13:02.156 --> 13:03.199
He did.

13:03.283 --> 13:07.203
When he showed up like that,
you should've run or screamed.

13:07.287 --> 13:10.331
That's what you should've done.
You're not who you used to be.

13:10.999 --> 13:12.250
I know that.

13:13.960 --> 13:16.879
It was so unexpected.
I think I just froze.

13:18.506 --> 13:22.760
Still, you shouldn't have
run out mid-game.

13:22.844 --> 13:25.638
It's not like something bad
was going to happen right away.

13:27.473 --> 13:28.558
Si-yeol.

13:33.104 --> 13:34.439
I was so scared.

13:44.741 --> 13:47.243
Seeing him there, right next to you,

13:48.828 --> 13:52.665
I couldn't think of anything else.
I was just scared.

13:53.708 --> 13:55.168
Honestly, I still am.

13:56.336 --> 13:58.921
There's nothing I can do
to protect you right now.

13:59.547 --> 14:02.091
If he tries
to pull something on you again,

14:02.175 --> 14:04.844
I don't even know what I should do.

14:09.432 --> 14:10.600
Don't worry.

14:11.642 --> 14:13.644
Looks like they found out

14:14.270 --> 14:18.274
that I became human
and that I'm trying to change back.

14:19.150 --> 14:22.028
Worst case, I can ask
the eight-tailed fox for help.

14:22.653 --> 14:24.280
It'll be fine.

14:29.786 --> 14:30.912
It's okay.

14:33.081 --> 14:34.290
Sis.

14:36.834 --> 14:38.711
Can you really not hear me?

15:02.402 --> 15:04.404
What just happened?

15:05.196 --> 15:06.572
Wake up.

15:14.163 --> 15:16.499
Hand over your fox bead.

15:16.582 --> 15:18.751
I've got a good use for it.

15:21.129 --> 15:22.630
I'm afraid I can't do that.

15:23.881 --> 15:25.091
What?

15:25.174 --> 15:26.843
My fox bead

15:28.219 --> 15:29.720
isn't on me right now.

15:33.015 --> 15:34.350
Seriously, what do I do?

15:35.435 --> 15:38.688
I already told him where my fox bead is.

15:40.189 --> 15:43.568
And I can't even warn her to be careful.

15:43.651 --> 15:46.362
Let's move as soon as we get to Seoul.

15:47.238 --> 15:49.615
It's way too cramped
and uncomfortable anyway.

15:50.241 --> 15:53.494
And then, we'll get you
back to normal as soon as…

15:53.995 --> 15:55.538
- Wait a second.
- Yeah?

15:56.080 --> 15:59.667
Have you always had that sweater?

16:00.460 --> 16:01.627
You mean this?

16:02.295 --> 16:05.756
I found it while packing. Is it weird?

16:06.299 --> 16:07.967
No, it's just…

16:09.051 --> 16:10.887
I've just never seen it before.

16:10.970 --> 16:13.931
I've had this for a really long time.

16:14.015 --> 16:15.475
My grandma bought it for me.

16:23.274 --> 16:25.401
So it wasn't a dream.

16:26.736 --> 16:31.991
It's a future I can't change or avoid.

16:32.074 --> 16:34.327
Are you telling me to choose?

16:34.410 --> 16:38.831
Kill Si-yeol, or give up who I am?

16:39.457 --> 16:41.167
It may seem cruel,

16:41.250 --> 16:43.794
but fate simply takes its course.

16:43.878 --> 16:47.381
It does not concern itself
with individual human affairs.

16:47.465 --> 16:51.552
Once the storm rises,
everyone gets swept away.

16:51.636 --> 16:55.765
Can you truly handle that for a lifetime?

16:58.184 --> 16:59.435
Si-yeol.

16:59.519 --> 17:02.813
What exactly are we being swept up in

17:03.814 --> 17:06.150
to face a future like that?

17:08.861 --> 17:11.155
Why would you…

17:13.741 --> 17:14.784
Si-yeol.

17:15.785 --> 17:17.036
I can't do this.

17:18.538 --> 17:20.706
- What?
- I've been thinking…

17:22.583 --> 17:24.835
and I don't want to just leave like this.

17:24.919 --> 17:26.337
We came here for a trip.

17:26.420 --> 17:29.048
I don't want to just run away
like we're being chased.

17:30.216 --> 17:31.551
Let's get off this train.

17:35.972 --> 17:39.517
They say this village has been here
since the Joseon Dynasty.

17:40.059 --> 17:43.187
Even these thatched houses
are hundreds of years old--

17:43.271 --> 17:45.356
Did you forget who I am?

17:46.065 --> 17:47.233
What?

17:47.316 --> 17:50.319
I used to live in places like this
back in the day.

17:50.403 --> 17:54.907
You call this a tourist spot?
It's just a regular village.

17:55.825 --> 17:57.910
Oh, right.

18:00.663 --> 18:04.375
I saw that this was a famous tourist spot
around here.

18:05.251 --> 18:08.671
- Should we go somewhere else?
- No, we came all this way.

18:09.213 --> 18:11.924
Come on, let's look around.

18:13.843 --> 18:14.927
Oh man…

18:31.110 --> 18:32.111
Si-yeol.

18:32.862 --> 18:35.156
Give the roof a little shake
with that stick.

18:35.239 --> 18:37.491
The roof? Why?

18:37.575 --> 18:39.035
To make the grubs fall down.

18:39.744 --> 18:43.456
They should be nice and plump
right about now.

18:43.539 --> 18:47.752
What? Aren't grubs bugs?
What would you need them for?

18:47.835 --> 18:50.338
Since we're here,
you should try them as a snack.

18:51.130 --> 18:53.341
No way. What are you talking about?

18:53.424 --> 18:55.593
Try it. Do you want me to catch one?

18:56.260 --> 18:58.304
You don't have to. I said no.

18:58.387 --> 18:59.930
They taste better than you think.

19:00.014 --> 19:03.517
Back in the day, old folks used to use
grubs as medicine, you know?

19:03.601 --> 19:05.895
- I'll catch one for you.
- Wait…

19:08.648 --> 19:10.024
What…

19:14.987 --> 19:16.489
Hey, don't. Don't do it!

19:16.572 --> 19:19.408
- Why? I'll get you a grub.
- Forget the grub.

19:19.492 --> 19:22.119
But we came all this way.
You have to try it.

19:22.203 --> 19:24.288
Wait, just put it down. Seriously.

19:24.372 --> 19:26.499
Come on, you should have a taste.

19:26.582 --> 19:27.667
Hey, I'm not eating it!

19:27.750 --> 19:28.793
SAMSHIN

19:28.876 --> 19:32.296
Samshin. Like this.

19:33.964 --> 19:35.633
Do this one too.

19:35.716 --> 19:37.093
- I'm not doing it anymore.
- Come on.

19:37.176 --> 19:39.261
Forget it, I'm done.

19:39.345 --> 19:40.221
I'm not doing it.

19:43.933 --> 19:46.686
- Here, lie down.
- What? No way.

19:46.769 --> 19:50.481
- Please lie down, just once.
- No, let's just look around and go.

19:51.107 --> 19:53.401
Come on, just lie down once.

19:53.484 --> 19:55.319
- Please?
- No. You're going to hit me.

19:55.403 --> 19:56.570
No, wait.

19:56.654 --> 19:57.530
Hey!

20:07.206 --> 20:08.749
- What?
- Nice!

20:08.833 --> 20:10.501
- Give me your palm.
- No. Let's do it again.

20:10.584 --> 20:12.294
- Come on, give me your wrist.
- No!

20:12.962 --> 20:15.339
Hey, what are you doing?
You can't throw it like that!

20:15.423 --> 20:17.299
Oh my. Look at this.

20:18.259 --> 20:20.386
Wow, look at this place.

20:21.887 --> 20:23.556
Si-yeol, do you know what this is?

20:23.639 --> 20:26.267
- What is it?
- It's cotton.

20:26.350 --> 20:28.477
Do you know how to make clothes out of it?

20:28.561 --> 20:30.521
First, you take out the cotton seeds.

20:30.604 --> 20:33.441
You take out the seed, and then there's
something called a cotton bow.

20:33.524 --> 20:36.736
And if you beat the seeds with that,
it puffs up like cotton.

20:36.819 --> 20:40.656
Then you take a handful of it,
put it on a sorghum stalk, and spin it…

20:44.994 --> 20:47.246
Here you go.

20:57.757 --> 20:58.799
Open wide.

21:02.428 --> 21:03.888
Mm! It's good.

21:10.978 --> 21:13.856
- It's good, right?
- It's even better because you fed me.

21:13.939 --> 21:15.191
Gosh, stop it.

21:48.516 --> 21:49.767
What's with the sudden photo?

21:50.935 --> 21:53.437
Oh, I just thought you looked pretty.

21:54.271 --> 21:55.272
Gosh.

21:57.817 --> 22:00.486
Take it again. I wasn't ready.

22:03.989 --> 22:04.907
You look so pretty.

22:07.743 --> 22:09.703
It came out well. Let me show you.

22:12.998 --> 22:14.792
It did come out well!

22:19.672 --> 22:22.341
You should stand here too.
This looks like a good photo spot.

22:22.424 --> 22:24.635
Actually, why don't we take one together?

22:24.718 --> 22:26.887
- What?
- Come to think of it,

22:26.971 --> 22:29.014
we don't have any photos together.

22:31.559 --> 22:32.560
- Excuse me.
- Yes?

22:32.643 --> 22:34.812
- Could you take a photo of us?
- Sure.

22:37.356 --> 22:38.607
Are you ready?

22:39.275 --> 22:41.277
One, two, three.

22:51.120 --> 22:53.038
Oh, jeez!

22:53.539 --> 22:55.499
You scared the hell out of me.

22:55.583 --> 22:56.542
Seriously.

22:57.042 --> 23:00.379
You can't just walk in here. Damn it.

23:03.507 --> 23:04.508
What is it?

23:05.551 --> 23:08.721
You look like you're already
halfway to the grave.

23:11.140 --> 23:14.476
Catching that other fox
must've been tough on you.

23:14.560 --> 23:15.644
Not yet.

23:16.729 --> 23:19.315
- What?
- I said it's not over.

23:19.398 --> 23:21.025
I couldn't get the fox bead.

23:22.109 --> 23:23.485
What are you talking about?

23:24.403 --> 23:26.614
Then nothing's changed at all.

23:26.697 --> 23:28.073
Jeez.

23:29.575 --> 23:32.953
I went to that former nine-tailed fox
and made all sorts of threats.

23:33.037 --> 23:37.082
If that other monster is still with her,
what am I supposed to do now?

23:37.958 --> 23:40.044
No need to get so worked up.

23:40.586 --> 23:44.340
How can I not get worked up?

23:44.423 --> 23:46.425
You took two billion won from me.

23:47.509 --> 23:52.473
If that other fox is still with her,
do you really think she'll let me be?

23:53.557 --> 23:55.059
You really are a coward.

23:56.685 --> 23:59.730
I bewitched the Seoraksan Mountain fox,
just as planned.

23:59.813 --> 24:01.315
But in exchange,

24:01.941 --> 24:03.734
I burned up all my shamanic power

24:04.693 --> 24:07.237
when I already don't have much time left.

24:07.905 --> 24:10.449
So what's going to happen now?

24:10.532 --> 24:12.368
I'll be dead soon,

24:12.451 --> 24:15.371
unless I find and swallow that fox bead
in the next few days.

24:17.331 --> 24:19.750
That's your problem. But what about me?

24:20.501 --> 24:21.835
What's going to happen to me?

24:23.587 --> 24:25.673
Figure that one out yourself, you punk.

24:27.383 --> 24:31.303
But if you're scared of that fox
sticking around her,

24:31.387 --> 24:33.514
you don't need to worry
about that anymore.

24:34.056 --> 24:36.892
She's just a puppet now,
and she can only do what I tell her.

24:36.976 --> 24:39.228
She'll stay that way until I die.

24:40.688 --> 24:43.732
Really? Are you sure
I don't have to worry about it?

24:44.358 --> 24:48.195
Yes. I ordered her
to go fetch the fox bead herself.

24:48.278 --> 24:49.989
You can see for yourself then…

24:51.115 --> 24:54.243
whether that fox does
what I tell her to do or not.

25:10.300 --> 25:11.343
This is nice.

25:12.302 --> 25:13.595
I'm glad.

25:14.138 --> 25:16.306
I thought today's trip was a total bust

25:16.890 --> 25:18.934
because I took you to a Joseon-era village

25:19.018 --> 25:20.769
when you lived through that era.

25:22.521 --> 25:24.898
Walking through that old village with you

25:25.566 --> 25:29.820
made me feel
like we've known each other forever.

25:30.696 --> 25:31.905
I liked that.

25:33.991 --> 25:36.910
It felt like you became
a small part of all those years

25:37.494 --> 25:39.872
I spent alone in my past.

25:41.832 --> 25:45.044
Next time, let's go somewhere better.
Somewhere you've never been.

25:45.711 --> 25:50.841
Then I can be part of your past
and your future, right?

25:50.924 --> 25:54.762
Yeah. That'd be really nice.

26:02.895 --> 26:03.896
Si-yeol.

26:06.982 --> 26:08.275
Should we just…

26:10.069 --> 26:13.447
stay like this and not go back?

26:14.073 --> 26:14.948
What?

26:15.032 --> 26:16.950
I could just be an ordinary human.

26:17.034 --> 26:20.537
And instead of being the famous
Kang Si-yeol that everyone knows,

26:21.955 --> 26:25.000
you'd stay a fourth-division player,
just like now.

26:34.760 --> 26:35.636
Hey.

26:35.719 --> 26:37.471
I was just joking,

26:38.013 --> 26:42.017
but you went all quiet,
and now it feels way too serious.

26:44.103 --> 26:45.896
Okay. Let's do it.

26:49.441 --> 26:50.442
What?

26:50.526 --> 26:53.112
If that's what you want, let's do it.

26:55.906 --> 26:58.784
Are you really okay living like this?

26:59.910 --> 27:02.287
Your dreams, your hard work,
and everything you've achieved

27:02.371 --> 27:03.997
are not part of this life.

27:04.081 --> 27:05.791
How can you be okay with that?

27:05.874 --> 27:07.501
And you saw what happened earlier.

27:07.584 --> 27:10.963
People with a grudge against me
are coming after you too.

27:11.046 --> 27:14.591
If we stay like this,
it won't be a normal life.

27:15.843 --> 27:18.554
We might have to spend our lives
looking over our shoulders.

27:20.514 --> 27:22.558
I'm not saying it would be okay.

27:22.641 --> 27:25.060
I'm saying I'm okay with it not being okay

27:27.563 --> 27:29.064
What does that even--

27:29.148 --> 27:31.400
I know you're hiding something from me.

27:32.818 --> 27:36.071
Ever since we came back
from visiting Woo-seok at the hospital,

27:36.155 --> 27:37.614
you've been acting weird.

27:38.699 --> 27:40.117
I don't know what it is,

27:40.742 --> 27:41.827
but knowing you,

27:41.910 --> 27:44.538
you'd have told me already
if it wasn't a big deal.

27:44.621 --> 27:47.374
You're struggling alone,
and you can't even tell me,

27:48.250 --> 27:50.419
so it must be a problem we can't solve.

27:51.962 --> 27:53.046
Si-yeol…

27:53.130 --> 27:55.174
If it's a matter of choice,

27:56.175 --> 27:58.594
of course I want to go back
to how things were.

27:59.386 --> 28:04.349
Like you said, my life, my hard work,
the dreams that I achieved

28:05.642 --> 28:07.311
all mean a great deal to me.

28:08.437 --> 28:09.479
However,

28:10.480 --> 28:12.232
if you try your best

28:12.316 --> 28:15.319
to change things back and still can't,

28:16.361 --> 28:17.613
it's okay.

28:18.238 --> 28:19.531
I'll just accept it.

28:24.036 --> 28:26.997
It's not over yet, and I haven't given up.

28:27.748 --> 28:33.128
I'll keep trying to find the best solution
for both of us until the very last moment.

28:34.922 --> 28:35.923
I know.

28:42.179 --> 28:44.181
But I'm scared.

28:45.724 --> 28:47.935
I'm scared that we'll get swept away

28:49.019 --> 28:50.979
by fate or that damn will of Heaven.

28:52.981 --> 28:54.066
I'm scared…

28:56.068 --> 28:58.237
that I won't be able to protect us.

29:01.615 --> 29:02.950
Si-yeol,

29:04.243 --> 29:05.369
I think…

29:08.247 --> 29:10.707
I really like you.

29:53.917 --> 29:55.127
What?

29:57.546 --> 30:00.549
I specifically asked for twin beds,

30:01.174 --> 30:02.718
but it's a double.

30:09.641 --> 30:12.394
Maybe we should've
just gone back to Seoul.

30:12.477 --> 30:14.688
Yeah, maybe.

30:17.149 --> 30:19.735
But then again, we are on a trip.

30:20.652 --> 30:22.821
Right. And it's late.

30:23.447 --> 30:27.117
- And we're tired from all the walking.
- Yeah, that's right.

30:27.200 --> 30:28.702
Yeah.

30:31.330 --> 30:34.249
Do you want to look around?

30:35.709 --> 30:36.668
Sure.

30:37.169 --> 30:39.963
- Yeah.
- Yeah.

30:43.800 --> 30:45.093
Here, give me that.

30:45.635 --> 30:48.055
Yeah, okay.

31:00.150 --> 31:01.193
Hey,

31:01.276 --> 31:03.111
we've been living in the same house.

31:03.195 --> 31:05.364
Why are you being so awkward?

31:06.448 --> 31:08.950
Who, me? I'm not being awkward.

31:10.202 --> 31:11.870
Seriously, I'm not.

31:12.704 --> 31:13.830
Maybe you're feeling awkward.

31:16.458 --> 31:18.794
Not at all. I don't feel awkward.

31:32.557 --> 31:33.558
Oh, right.

31:34.226 --> 31:36.311
I should ask them to switch rooms.

31:45.195 --> 31:46.196
It's fine.

31:47.948 --> 31:48.990
What?

31:49.616 --> 31:52.411
I mean, this room is actually really nice.

31:55.872 --> 31:57.999
It's got an ocean view and everything.

32:00.919 --> 32:03.797
So, you don't have to go ask.

32:12.556 --> 32:13.723
You told me not to, okay?

32:16.560 --> 32:17.602
What?

33:06.359 --> 33:07.486
I love you.

33:51.988 --> 33:54.074
- Are you awake?
- Yeah.

33:54.616 --> 33:55.659
When did you wake up?

33:56.535 --> 33:57.619
Just now.

34:02.624 --> 34:05.627
- Do you want to sleep a bit longer?
- Yeah, just a little.

34:13.802 --> 34:14.970
But seriously…

34:16.012 --> 34:17.389
I just don't get him.

34:17.472 --> 34:21.059
He's a lunatic. Why did he have to
drag us down with him?

34:25.564 --> 34:28.942
And why is he skipping training
like he's done nothing wrong?

34:30.318 --> 34:31.736
Forget all that.

34:32.237 --> 34:34.698
Is there even any point
in training like this?

34:34.781 --> 34:37.325
Most of us can't even transfer anywhere.

34:37.409 --> 34:39.160
We're all just
going to be forced to retire.

34:39.244 --> 34:43.290
I knew Si-yeol
would eventually mess up big time.

34:43.373 --> 34:44.833
Man, I'm tired.

34:44.916 --> 34:48.128
I was so stressed that
I couldn't get a wink of sleep last night.

34:52.257 --> 34:53.967
- Want one?
- Thanks.

34:54.593 --> 34:55.885
Give me one too.

34:58.305 --> 34:59.514
It's kicking in now.

35:00.724 --> 35:02.684
Man, caffeine really helps.

35:02.767 --> 35:04.519
I'm done with Si-yeol.

35:05.770 --> 35:07.230
- Seriously?
- Yeah.

35:07.856 --> 35:10.942
I mean, if he messed up that badly,

35:11.026 --> 35:12.902
he should be begging
the owner for forgiveness.

35:12.986 --> 35:14.321
Or at least try to fix it.

35:14.404 --> 35:16.823
How can he ghost us instead?
I'm so pissed off.

35:19.451 --> 35:21.202
Should I try calling him or something?

35:21.286 --> 35:22.537
Forget it. Don't bother.

35:23.830 --> 35:25.206
Excuse me. Is the coach in?

35:25.290 --> 35:27.500
- Hello.
- Hello.

35:28.376 --> 35:29.878
Coach didn't come in today.

35:30.545 --> 35:32.589
Oh, really?

35:32.672 --> 35:33.882
What brings you here?

35:33.965 --> 35:35.592
Well, it's just…

35:36.092 --> 35:39.387
I think I know why Si-yeol
acted the way he did yesterday.

35:39.471 --> 35:41.723
I think I might have made a mistake.

35:41.806 --> 35:44.893
I can't believe
that I completely forgot about that.

35:45.810 --> 35:47.896
What do you mean?

35:49.689 --> 35:52.942
Are you sure
you don't need to go to training?

35:53.026 --> 35:55.236
How could I go anywhere
and leave you alone?

35:55.320 --> 35:57.906
I'm not leaving your side for a while.

35:58.406 --> 36:00.200
Jeez, I'm not a child.

36:01.242 --> 36:03.036
It's for the best, actually.

36:03.119 --> 36:05.914
Honestly, we don't have time
to be distracted by training and stuff.

36:05.997 --> 36:08.166
We need to find
the people you listed in your notebook,

36:08.249 --> 36:10.919
and find out where they are
and what they're doing.

36:11.252 --> 36:12.295
You're right.

36:14.130 --> 36:15.173
Oh, wait.

36:16.216 --> 36:17.717
You know that sweater from yesterday?

36:17.801 --> 36:19.678
- Yeah.
- Do you have it right now?

36:21.012 --> 36:22.555
Let's throw it away over there.

36:22.639 --> 36:24.808
What are you talking about?

36:24.891 --> 36:26.935
I told you my grandma bought me that.

36:27.018 --> 36:29.229
Is that the only thing
she ever bought you?

36:29.938 --> 36:31.731
No, I have a lot, but--

36:31.815 --> 36:35.568
Then throw it away. It looks weird,
and the color's wrong for you.

36:35.652 --> 36:37.070
Really, it doesn't suit you.

36:37.153 --> 36:40.448
What do you mean? It looks good on me.

36:44.536 --> 36:45.537
Throw it away.

36:47.997 --> 36:49.999
But it's perfectly fine.

36:51.042 --> 36:52.919
I really like this sweater.

36:53.628 --> 36:56.005
Well, I totally hate it.

36:58.174 --> 36:59.634
Should I throw it away?

37:00.677 --> 37:03.471
Man, that temper of yours. Fine.

37:08.727 --> 37:10.478
I was on edge all day yesterday,

37:10.562 --> 37:12.981
thinking something
would happen at any second.

37:13.064 --> 37:14.524
I should've done this sooner.

37:15.024 --> 37:16.317
What?

37:17.026 --> 37:18.027
Nothing.

37:30.081 --> 37:33.084
Why did we come all the way here?
He'll come out when he's ready.

37:33.168 --> 37:36.671
Come on, stop acting all tough
and just come along.

37:36.755 --> 37:38.631
We're already here anyway.

37:38.715 --> 37:41.718
Si-yeol should've told us that earlier.

37:41.801 --> 37:43.553
I would've lost it too

37:43.636 --> 37:47.682
if the guy who ruined my life
in a hit-and-run suddenly showed up.

37:48.308 --> 37:50.268
I looked him up on our way here.

37:50.351 --> 37:52.562
Turns out he's a murderer,
a total scumbag.

37:53.104 --> 37:56.858
We don't want a person like that
as our club owner, either.

37:56.941 --> 37:59.611
- Yeah.
- Si-yeol did the right thing this time.

38:01.154 --> 38:02.363
Si-yeol!

38:02.989 --> 38:04.240
Hey, Si-yeol!

38:05.200 --> 38:06.326
I don't think he's home.

38:06.409 --> 38:07.994
- Damn it.
- Man, it's cold.

38:08.077 --> 38:09.662
Let's just wait inside.

38:18.046 --> 38:19.047
What the heck?

38:19.964 --> 38:21.007
What happened?

38:22.467 --> 38:23.718
Hey.

38:25.678 --> 38:28.097
Looks like he really got robbed this time.

38:28.723 --> 38:32.060
Why are you standing out here?
You could've waited at home.

38:33.394 --> 38:34.562
Sis.

38:35.188 --> 38:36.439
Yeah?

38:36.523 --> 38:38.566
Give my fox bead back.

38:47.951 --> 38:48.910
Who are you?

38:50.537 --> 38:51.538
What?

39:06.177 --> 39:07.262
Wait.

39:07.345 --> 39:09.013
What do you think you're--

39:18.982 --> 39:20.650
Where is my fox bead?

39:21.317 --> 39:24.529
It wasn't at the house,
and you don't seem to have it on you.

39:24.612 --> 39:25.822
Where did you hide it?

39:25.905 --> 39:29.033
What if I give it to you?
Who are you offering it to?

39:29.659 --> 39:31.536
Don't you know what'll happen to you then?

39:31.619 --> 39:32.912
It's mine.

39:33.413 --> 39:36.165
However I use it is up to me.

39:36.249 --> 39:37.625
Snap out of it.

39:38.293 --> 39:39.961
Did you forget what I told you?

39:41.170 --> 39:44.799
I don't know what that damn shaman did,

39:44.883 --> 39:47.135
but you're just an empty shell,
and the real you is gone--

39:47.218 --> 39:48.595
I guess I have no choice.

39:48.678 --> 39:51.514
For some reason,
I can't even feel the bead's energy.

39:51.598 --> 39:53.808
And it seems like you won't just tell me…

39:55.768 --> 39:57.729
so I'll have to find out for myself.

40:14.746 --> 40:16.539
What are you staring at?

40:18.082 --> 40:19.292
Your family.

40:20.376 --> 40:23.171
Family? Way to kill the mood.

40:25.381 --> 40:28.092
Anyway, how much longer do I have to wait?

40:28.927 --> 40:30.011
It won't be long.

40:30.094 --> 40:33.640
I doubt I'll have any time left
after tonight anyway.

40:34.474 --> 40:36.184
You might not know this,

40:37.685 --> 40:39.103
but in here,

40:40.021 --> 40:44.025
there are all sorts of minor spirits
that hold a grudge against me.

40:45.610 --> 40:50.156
They're just waiting for me to die
so they can rip my soul to pieces.

40:51.240 --> 40:52.784
Why say things like that

40:52.867 --> 40:55.912
to someone living a normal life,
unaware of such things?

40:56.663 --> 40:58.957
I used to live blissfully unaware too.

41:02.627 --> 41:04.420
If you get that fox bead,

41:05.129 --> 41:07.507
does that mean you won't die today?

41:08.675 --> 41:09.759
No.

41:11.344 --> 41:12.637
It's more than that.

41:13.179 --> 41:15.056
I'll become immortal.

41:15.890 --> 41:16.849
What do you mean…

41:18.893 --> 41:20.228
I'm going to become a deity.

41:20.853 --> 41:21.729
What?

41:21.813 --> 41:25.900
Spiritual beings like the nine-tailed fox
are like demigods, not mere animals.

41:25.984 --> 41:29.570
So if I steal their fox bead
and swallow it,

41:30.405 --> 41:33.700
I can shed this human form
and become a deity.

41:35.702 --> 41:39.205
So? What's your plan
after becoming immortal?

41:40.164 --> 41:41.124
Revenge.

41:42.083 --> 41:44.544
You must know roughly
what happened to my family,

41:44.627 --> 41:46.629
since you did some digging on me.

41:47.588 --> 41:48.464
Yeah, roughly.

41:49.507 --> 41:51.175
Just that you refused
the shamanic calling,

41:51.259 --> 41:53.386
and that's why your whole family
ended up that way.

41:53.469 --> 41:57.473
At least my wife died quickly.
It was a car accident.

41:57.557 --> 41:59.559
I was the one behind the wheel,

41:59.642 --> 42:02.562
and I slammed
right into an oncoming truck.

42:02.645 --> 42:04.814
It was like I was possessed.

42:04.897 --> 42:07.150
I didn't have control over my body.

42:09.527 --> 42:11.320
The car was completely destroyed.

42:11.404 --> 42:14.699
My wife was torn to pieces
right there on impact.

42:14.782 --> 42:19.287
But I was in the driver's seat
and didn't have a single scratch on me.

42:19.370 --> 42:22.331
Since I was their vessel,
they needed me unharmed.

42:23.416 --> 42:25.668
So you finally accepted
the shamanic calling?

42:25.752 --> 42:26.919
No.

42:28.671 --> 42:31.382
Even then,
I cared more about my own life.

42:32.133 --> 42:34.343
So they went after my daughter.

42:36.888 --> 42:38.556
It started out of nowhere.

42:38.639 --> 42:41.642
She was in so much pain,
like she was dying.

42:42.393 --> 42:44.771
But the doctors couldn't find a cause.

42:46.814 --> 42:50.985
I was desperate to save her,
so I tried everything and went everywhere.

42:51.819 --> 42:53.821
Then, she just couldn't take it anymore.

42:54.906 --> 42:58.117
She took her own life
because she wanted the pain to stop.

42:58.868 --> 43:02.622
Is it even possible to get revenge
on those beings?

43:03.831 --> 43:07.460
Of course. Starting with the deity
that did this to us,

43:07.543 --> 43:11.089
I devoured all sorts of minor spirits.

43:11.172 --> 43:14.258
It took me years,
but I hunted them down, one by one.

43:15.259 --> 43:16.677
These marks are the seals.

43:18.971 --> 43:21.766
They don't control me anymore.

43:22.266 --> 43:24.602
I'm the one who controls them.

43:25.394 --> 43:29.148
Wait. Then you already got your revenge.

43:29.232 --> 43:31.943
No. This isn't just about
these minor spirits.

43:32.568 --> 43:36.405
I'm talking about the greater deities
who created a world like this, and…

43:38.032 --> 43:41.744
even this damn world itself.
I'll destroy them all.

43:42.370 --> 43:43.996
I'll live 100 or 1,000 years if necessary.

43:44.080 --> 43:47.625
And if even that isn't enough,
I'll live 10,000 years to see it through.

44:05.476 --> 44:06.853
How is this…

44:21.534 --> 44:23.369
How did I get home?

44:25.538 --> 44:27.456
I was just…

44:31.752 --> 44:33.588
What was I doing again?

44:54.692 --> 44:56.027
Eun-ho!

45:00.907 --> 45:02.033
Geum-ho?

45:02.116 --> 45:04.994
Shopping just isn't fun without you.

45:06.454 --> 45:09.540
We could've grabbed lunch and some coffee.

45:09.624 --> 45:11.292
You really should've come along.

45:11.918 --> 45:13.669
What were you doing here all alone?

45:15.129 --> 45:16.130
Well,

45:16.964 --> 45:18.549
I was just…

45:21.969 --> 45:23.012
But, Geum-ho…

45:24.639 --> 45:25.681
is it really you?

45:27.308 --> 45:29.518
- What?
- I mean, I swear

45:29.602 --> 45:32.396
you became human centuries ago.

45:32.480 --> 45:34.315
And you got married,

45:35.316 --> 45:36.484
then…

45:38.444 --> 45:39.570
you died.

45:40.238 --> 45:42.573
What are you talking about?
Did you have a dream?

45:44.575 --> 45:45.576
A dream?

45:45.660 --> 45:47.245
Forget about that.

45:49.372 --> 45:50.456
Here, try this on.

45:51.082 --> 45:53.751
I bought it because I thought
it'd look good on you.

46:01.467 --> 46:03.135
It must've been a dream.

46:04.428 --> 46:06.389
Come on. You're not a child.

46:07.181 --> 46:09.058
What kind of dream was it?

46:11.102 --> 46:12.395
I'm not really sure.

46:13.271 --> 46:15.648
It felt so vivid, so real.

46:15.731 --> 46:18.025
But now that I'm awake,
I can't remember much.

46:19.860 --> 46:21.445
Just that you weren't with me

46:22.154 --> 46:24.991
and I was alone for a very long time.

46:26.826 --> 46:29.036
I think there was someone else too.

46:30.997 --> 46:33.374
It was just a silly dream. Let's eat.

46:33.457 --> 46:35.293
I picked up some takeout for us.

46:38.504 --> 46:40.423
I mean, it was a really strange dream.

46:40.506 --> 46:44.927
I became a human,
and I think I even dated a man.

46:46.012 --> 46:48.014
You dated a human?

46:48.556 --> 46:50.599
What kind of guy was he?

46:51.600 --> 46:53.936
I don't know. I can't remember that part.

46:56.230 --> 46:57.732
Was he handsome?

46:58.524 --> 47:01.986
His face was so clear in the dream,

47:02.069 --> 47:03.738
but now I can't really recall.

47:03.821 --> 47:04.989
By the way, Eun-ho.

47:05.072 --> 47:08.117
You know the thing I left with you?
Where is it?

47:08.993 --> 47:09.952
What?

47:10.036 --> 47:11.620
My fox bead.

47:12.913 --> 47:14.081
You have it.

47:18.085 --> 47:20.004
Why would I have that?

47:21.297 --> 47:23.257
Wait, do I?

47:26.302 --> 47:28.179
Where did I put it?

47:30.848 --> 47:31.891
Think carefully.

47:42.443 --> 47:43.861
This place is…

47:44.653 --> 47:47.615
So, my bead is here?

47:49.617 --> 47:53.245
Yeah. Why did I keep it here again?

47:56.248 --> 47:58.793
Oh, right. It was because…

47:59.460 --> 48:00.628
Sis, snap out of it.

48:01.462 --> 48:04.173
Don't tell her anything. This is all fake.

48:04.840 --> 48:05.841
"Sis"?

48:06.717 --> 48:09.553
Wait, she's not Geum-ho?

48:10.304 --> 48:13.349
Eun-ho, don't overthink it.

48:13.432 --> 48:16.435
Just tell me where you hid the fox bead--

48:16.519 --> 48:18.020
Sis, can't you hear that voice?

48:18.813 --> 48:19.814
A voice?

48:21.399 --> 48:24.652
Eun-ho, wake up!

48:25.653 --> 48:26.987
Eun-ho.

48:27.071 --> 48:28.531
- Eun-ho.
- Si-yeol?

48:29.156 --> 48:31.409
Eun-ho, come on. Wake up.

48:32.076 --> 48:34.078
I was almost there. What a hassle.

48:43.087 --> 48:45.297
Tell me where you're keeping my fox bead.

48:47.591 --> 48:49.176
It wasn't in that hospital room.

48:50.636 --> 48:51.762
Geum-ho.

48:55.891 --> 49:00.104
So you're saying
there are weird humans after my fox bead?

49:00.187 --> 49:03.149
Yeah, I heard it from Si-yeol's friend.

49:04.024 --> 49:07.445
Now that they know I'm human,
I think they're looking for you.

49:07.528 --> 49:10.990
But even if he is a shaman,
he's still just human.

49:11.490 --> 49:12.825
How dangerous can he be?

49:13.784 --> 49:17.163
I'm not sure, but we should
take precautions just in case.

49:18.330 --> 49:21.750
So, I'm going to hide your fox bead
without telling you where.

49:21.834 --> 49:26.046
How? Whether you keep it
or hide it somewhere,

49:26.130 --> 49:27.673
I'd be able to sense it.

49:29.550 --> 49:33.471
I need to sever your connection
to the bead, just for a while.

49:40.769 --> 49:42.021
You trust me, right?

49:47.651 --> 49:50.279
Eun-ho… Eun-ho!

49:51.906 --> 49:54.116
What am I supposed to do?

49:56.035 --> 49:59.288
The dagger. That should do it.

50:27.983 --> 50:28.943
This is…

50:29.026 --> 50:32.780
It's the only Sajin Ritual Blade
left in the world.

50:32.863 --> 50:35.741
It's a sacred dagger
that can sever and defy fate.

50:51.340 --> 50:53.551
You'll die at this rate.

50:54.301 --> 50:56.720
Wouldn't it be better
to just give me the bead?

50:57.721 --> 51:00.933
Tell him to put it in your hand. Quickly!

51:01.016 --> 51:02.726
- Hurry!
- In my hand?

51:12.403 --> 51:13.612
- In my hand…
- What?

51:16.031 --> 51:17.157
In my hand.

51:18.242 --> 51:19.451
In my hand…

52:04.580 --> 52:06.040
What's wrong?

52:09.293 --> 52:12.171
What's happening? Hey!

52:13.839 --> 52:16.216
- Something's wrong.
- What?

52:16.300 --> 52:17.635
The plan's ruined.

52:18.844 --> 52:20.387
Damn it.

52:21.263 --> 52:22.514
Hey!

52:27.603 --> 52:28.687
Eun-ho.

52:29.313 --> 52:31.732
Are you okay? Are you with me?

52:31.815 --> 52:33.484
- Sis.
- Si-yeol.

52:35.235 --> 52:37.946
Sis, are you okay?

52:39.698 --> 52:42.785
What happened? Why did you suddenly--

52:42.868 --> 52:44.078
It's all over.

52:45.162 --> 52:46.288
What?

52:47.623 --> 52:50.584
We're safe now.

52:58.759 --> 53:01.512
- Calm down!
- Get away!

53:01.595 --> 53:04.431
Get away from me!

53:05.683 --> 53:07.685
I don't have any power left.

53:07.768 --> 53:11.021
Just leave me alone!

53:13.273 --> 53:16.944
Damn it. Just… kill me!

53:17.027 --> 53:20.322
Just leave me alone to die.

53:21.240 --> 53:23.242
What the hell happened?

53:23.909 --> 53:28.747
Please, I was wrong. I'm sorry.

53:30.249 --> 53:32.000
I'm sorry.

53:32.751 --> 53:35.587
It was my fault. I was wrong.

53:51.687 --> 53:53.856
Man, cleaning everything up took forever.

53:53.939 --> 53:56.650
Are you sure nothing's missing?

53:57.901 --> 53:58.986
Yeah.

54:00.028 --> 54:02.656
Eun-ho seems pretty shaken up, though.

54:02.740 --> 54:04.158
Of course she is.

54:04.241 --> 54:06.702
The place was trashed
while they were gone.

54:07.661 --> 54:09.371
Anyway, let's get going.

54:09.455 --> 54:11.498
You rest up too, Si-yeol.
You must be pretty shaken.

54:11.582 --> 54:13.041
No, let's head out together.

54:13.792 --> 54:16.044
I need to get groceries
to make her something to eat.

54:16.128 --> 54:17.337
- Sure thing.
- Okay.

54:20.424 --> 54:21.967
Thanks.

54:46.074 --> 54:48.327
That'll be 22,980 won.

54:50.162 --> 54:52.539
Wait… what?

54:53.499 --> 54:56.168
Oh man. I forgot my wallet.

55:20.150 --> 55:22.611
I'm coming, okay?

55:22.694 --> 55:24.530
Who is it at this hour?

55:26.782 --> 55:27.783
What?

55:28.784 --> 55:30.494
And where did Si-yeol go?

55:32.287 --> 55:36.583
Gosh, all right! I'm coming!

55:44.925 --> 55:46.176
What are you doing?

55:46.802 --> 55:48.262
I was thinking about this all wrong.

55:48.345 --> 55:50.764
Forget waiting for my turn.

55:50.848 --> 55:52.266
Let's just end this right now.

55:55.561 --> 55:56.937
What do you think you're doing?

55:57.020 --> 55:59.565
If you're doing this
because you still trust that shaman--

55:59.648 --> 56:00.732
Trust who?

56:04.194 --> 56:06.947
That bastard's barely conscious.
He's just breathing with his eyes open.

56:07.030 --> 56:09.032
He's basically a vegetable.

56:09.116 --> 56:10.909
You guys did that to him!

56:13.662 --> 56:16.748
No. He brought that on himself.

56:17.791 --> 56:20.043
Just like you're doing right now.

56:21.086 --> 56:24.506
I don't care.
I'm not going to end up like that.

56:27.426 --> 56:28.594
This is the way of humans.

56:29.720 --> 56:33.140
Let's see if you can still use
that sorcery of yours

56:34.474 --> 56:36.226
with a hole in your head.

56:46.361 --> 56:47.404
Hey!

56:47.487 --> 56:48.655
You little--

57:00.083 --> 57:01.418
Si-yeol!

57:37.788 --> 57:39.206
Si-yeol…

57:40.082 --> 57:41.750
Si-yeol, why did you do that?

57:43.293 --> 57:44.336
Are you…

57:45.295 --> 57:46.338
Are you okay?

57:47.339 --> 57:51.885
Why are you worrying about me right now?
You're the one who got shot!

57:54.304 --> 57:56.515
This wasn't in the future I saw.

57:56.598 --> 57:59.559
Why is it you instead of me?

58:00.519 --> 58:02.854
He will eventually die.

58:03.480 --> 58:05.941
That's the fate

58:06.858 --> 58:08.026
you gave him.

58:10.612 --> 58:12.322
How can you do this?

58:13.073 --> 58:15.242
After you finally made me human

58:15.325 --> 58:18.704
and made me fall in love with a human,
how could you do this?

58:39.683 --> 58:41.184
Si-yeol.

58:42.519 --> 58:44.855
Si-yeol…

58:57.367 --> 58:59.619
No, Si-yeol… what do I do?

59:08.003 --> 59:09.880
SPECIAL APPEARANCE BY HONG SU-HYEON

59:34.279 --> 59:37.199
NO TAIL TO TELL

59:37.282 --> 59:39.659
- Please, save him.
- You can't come in.

59:39.743 --> 59:41.995
There will come a time
when you must choose.

59:42.079 --> 59:44.790
If Si-yeol just dies like this,

59:44.873 --> 59:46.792
then there's really nothing we can do.

59:46.875 --> 59:49.252
Even if I die, I want to die as myself.

59:50.712 --> 59:52.172
That's my wish.

59:52.255 --> 59:53.799
It's so strange

59:53.882 --> 59:57.928
that the only people left
who remember Eun-ho are you and me.

59:58.553 --> 01:00:01.515
You need to let go too.

01:00:02.015 --> 01:00:04.810
This is the end for me. My final moment.

01:00:04.893 --> 01:00:05.894
RIP KANG SI-YEOL

01:00:05.977 --> 01:00:08.230
I never once imagined an ending like this.

01:00:10.524 --> 01:00:12.526
Subtitle translation by Susanna Kim
